--- make
description: An enum in types/: a set of named values that typed parameters and fields only accept
category: Scripts and data
usage: <Name> [--values small,medium,large]
--values: The values, comma separated (default one, two, three)
example: kscript make enum Size --values small,medium,large
example: kscript make enum OrderStatus --values pending,paid,shipped,cancelled
to: {{ paths.types }}/{{ dir }}{{ kebab }}{{ ext }}
hint: Import it with import "{{ paths.types }}/{{ dir }}{{ kebab }}{{ ext }}", then use it as a type: fn pack(size: {{ pascal }})
---
/// {{ title }}.
enum {{ pascal }} { {{#each values}}{{ item | snake }}{{#unless last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}{{#unless values}}one, two, three{{/unless}} }
